# Deterministic four-GPU capacity trace for Qwen2-MoE-Tiny.
# capacity(t)=clip(round(2 + 1.3*sin(2*pi*t/180s)
#   + 0.7*sin(2*pi*t/70s) + burst(t)), 1, 4), seed-free and reproducible.
# The burst windows are +1 at 210-270s and 480-540s, -1 at 330-390s.
# This creates multi-node removes/adds, a one-worker floor interval, and a
# four-worker interval rather than alternating one remove with one add. The
# active set is rotated on pressure drops, so node-0 can be preempted while
# at least one Tiny worker remains ready; no event adds beyond node-0..node-3.
{"time_ms": 0, "event": "add", "nodes": ["node-0", "node-1"]}
{"time_ms": 30000, "event": "add", "nodes": ["node-2"]}
{"time_ms": 120000, "event": "add", "nodes": ["node-3"]}
{"time_ms": 120000, "event": "remove", "nodes": ["node-0", "node-1", "node-2"]}
{"time_ms": 180000, "event": "add", "nodes": ["node-0"]}
{"time_ms": 210000, "event": "add", "nodes": ["node-1", "node-2"]}
{"time_ms": 270000, "event": "remove", "nodes": ["node-3", "node-0", "node-1"]}
